{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"41bc18ce3b55aa2c","name":"card_unit_ki_45_dragon_slayer","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/BrothersInArms/units/card_unit_ki_45_dragon_slayer","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"Ki-45 DRAGON SLAYER","text":"Deployment: Becomes Veteran if this is the first Ki-45 DRAGON SLAYER you deploy this battle.","flavorText":"The Ki-45, also known as \"Nick\" by the Allies, was a twin-engine fighter aircraft developed during WWII. Its official name was \"Toryu,\" which means Dragon Slayer in Japanese. The Ki-45 was initially designed as a heavy fighter for the Imperial Japanese Army Air Service, intended to serve as both an interceptor and a bomber destroyer. It first flew in January 1939 and entered service in 1941. The usual weaponry of the Kawasaki Ki-45 Toryu included a 20mm cannon located in the nose, a 37mm cannon firing forwards from the fuselage, a 7.92mm machine gun that fired from the rear, and the capability to carry drop tanks or bombs under the wings. Other experimental armaments were also tested, such as the use of a 75mm cannon for assaulting ships. The Ki-45 was used in a variety of roles during the war, including as night fighter, interceptor, bomber escort, and fighter bomber aircraft. It was involved in many major battles, including the defense of the Japanese homeland during the Allied bombing campaign, as well as in the Pacific and Southeast Asia. Despite its formidable armament and performance, the Ki-45 suffered from a number of design flaws that limited its effectiveness and the aircraft's heavy armament and armor made it less maneuverable than other contemporary fighters. A total of 1,701 Ki-45’s were manufactured, including a few variants.","faction":"Japan","type":"fighter","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":4,"operationCost":2,"attack":4,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_ki_45_dragon_slayer","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_ki_45_dragon_slayer_title","SourceString":"Ki-45 DRAGON SLAYER","LocalizedString":"Ki-45 DRAGON SLAYER"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":4,"defense":3,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_ki_45_dragon_slayer_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Becomes Veteran if this is the first Ki-45 DRAGON SLAYER you deploy this battle.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Becomes Veteran if this is the first Ki-45 DRAGON SLAYER you deploy this battle."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_ki_45_dragon_slayer_history","SourceString":"The Ki-45, also known as \"Nick\" by the Allies, was a twin-engine fighter aircraft developed during WWII. Its official name was \"Toryu,\" which means Dragon Slayer in Japanese. The Ki-45 was initially designed as a heavy fighter for the Imperial Japanese Army Air Service, intended to serve as both an interceptor and a bomber destroyer. It first flew in January 1939 and entered service in 1941. The usual weaponry of the Kawasaki Ki-45 Toryu included a 20mm cannon located in the nose, a 37mm cannon firing forwards from the fuselage, a 7.92mm machine gun that fired from the rear, and the capability to carry drop tanks or bombs under the wings. Other experimental armaments were also tested, such as the use of a 75mm cannon for assaulting ships. The Ki-45 was used in a variety of roles during the war, including as night fighter, interceptor, bomber escort, and fighter bomber aircraft. It was involved in many major battles, including the defense of the Japanese homeland during the Allied bombing campaign, as well as in the Pacific and Southeast Asia. Despite its formidable armament and performance, the Ki-45 suffered from a number of design flaws that limited its effectiveness and the aircraft's heavy armament and armor made it less maneuverable than other contemporary fighters. A total of 1,701 Ki-45’s were manufactured, including a few variants.","LocalizedString":"The Ki-45, also known as \"Nick\" by the Allies, was a twin-engine fighter aircraft developed during WWII. Its official name was \"Toryu,\" which means Dragon Slayer in Japanese. The Ki-45 was initially designed as a heavy fighter for the Imperial Japanese Army Air Service, intended to serve as both an interceptor and a bomber destroyer. It first flew in January 1939 and entered service in 1941. The usual weaponry of the Kawasaki Ki-45 Toryu included a 20mm cannon located in the nose, a 37mm cannon firing forwards from the fuselage, a 7.92mm machine gun that fired from the rear, and the capability to carry drop tanks or bombs under the wings. Other experimental armaments were also tested, such as the use of a 75mm cannon for assaulting ships. The Ki-45 was used in a variety of roles during the war, including as night fighter, interceptor, bomber escort, and fighter bomber aircraft. It was involved in many major battles, including the defense of the Japanese homeland during the Allied bombing campaign, as well as in the Pacific and Southeast Asia. Despite its formidable armament and performance, the Ki-45 suffered from a number of design flaws that limited its effectiveness and the aircraft's heavy armament and armor made it less maneuverable than other contemporary fighters. A total of 1,701 Ki-45’s were manufactured, including a few variants."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BrothersInArms","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardCreatedAlterCard"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Veteran"],"draftBaseWeight":0.9,"hasDeployment":true,"spawnCardName":"card_unit_ki_45_dragon_slayer_vet","soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Card_Blowups/AU_Exp_Aircraft_Medium_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/Spring2023Candidates/t_dragon_slayer.t_dragon_slayer","SubPathStrin